WHAT A PLUGIN-DECLARED CONFIG FIELD WOULD REQUIRE (the mechanical answer to Q4). Today's checklist for one knob is 4 hand-maintained declarations — dataclass field (run.py:713-968) + validate_config check (1399-1603) + _FIELD_META entry (1654-1857) + argparse flag AND its threading into the single PipelineConfig(...) call (3815-3978 / 4014-4078) — plus an optional 5th (GUI CONFIG_SPEC gui/server.py:82-690) and 6th (CLI_PRESETS run.py:1377-1396, argparse-dest-keyed). Only steps 1-3 flow automatically downstream (schema -> GUI advanced panel -> copilot -> manifest -> replay). To let a PLUGIN declare fields with the same automatic flow, four things must change and none is deep:
 (a) config_schema() must merge dataclasses.fields(PipelineConfig) with a sorted list of plugin-declared field descriptors instead of returning only the former (run.py:1860-1888);
 (b) validate_config must call a per-plugin validate(cfg_section) after its own checks and before the _PROB_FIELDS clamp (run.py:1601-1603) — plugins get their own validator rather than adding ifs to the 200-line block;
 (c) config_from_dict must stop dropping unknown keys (run.py:1902-1904) and instead route a namespaced `plugins: {<id>: {version, config}}` section to the declaring plugin, FAILING when the plugin is absent or version-mismatched — otherwise the manifest contract silently breaks;
 (d) the CLI must generate flags from the schema rather than hand-declaring them (the schema already carries type/default/help/min/max/step/unit and widget), which simultaneously deletes the argparse/threading drift class the test suite currently polices (tests/test_gui_cli_contract.py, test_gui_curated_knobs.py) and the pf_* CONFIG_SPEC duplication (the gui-config-surface report's own 'kill the quadruple declaration' opportunity). A namespaced `--plugin.<id>.<field>` convention avoids collisions with the 138 flat fields.
The manifest also needs a plugins block recording, per plugin, its id, version, distribution, and a hash of its source or wheel — without that, constraint (2) (replayable from manifest.json) cannot hold for a plugin-configured run, and constraint (1) (pinned digests) has no way to attribute a digest change.

